-Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Auto-seed pan-African reference data on startup
-
-Country/RevenueAuthority/Language tables were only ever populated by
-manually running seed_pan_african_data.py. Since it was never (or only
-partially) run against the live DB, countries present in
-african_currencies.py -- like Burkina Faso -- weren't in the DB's
-Country table, causing 'Unknown country' errors when saving an account
-during registration.
-
-seed_all_pan_african_data() is idempotent (each seed function skips
-rows that already exist), so it's now called on every app startup
-right after run_migrations(), the same self-healing pattern already
-used for schema changes.
